    <string name="settings_bia_info_title">Why does the scale need this?</string>
    <string name="settings_bia_info_body">The scale computes body fat itself, and it needs your sex, your age and your height to do it. It is told these before every weigh-in.

Without them there is no measurement at all: an invented figure would come back looking plausible, and would then be stored as if it were yours.

The date of birth is stored rather than the age, so that it never silently goes out of date.</string>
